    "$10\\sqrt{5}$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "$50 = 25 \\cdot 2$, and $\\sqrt{25} = 5$, so $\\sqrt{50} = 5\\sqrt{2}$."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "easy",
   "prompt": "Simplify $\\sqrt{72}$.",
   "choices": [
    "$6\\sqrt{2}$",
    "$4\\sqrt{3}$",
    "$8\\sqrt{2}$",
    "$3\\sqrt{6}$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "$72 = 36 \\cdot 2$, so $\\sqrt{72} = 6\\sqrt{2}$. Always pull out the largest perfect square."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "easy",
   "prompt": "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{54}$.",
   "choices": [
    "$3\\sqrt[3]{2}$",
