   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "$54 = 27 \\cdot 2$ and $\\sqrt[3]{27} = 3$, so $\\sqrt[3]{54} = 3\\sqrt[3]{2}$."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "easy",
   "prompt": "Simplify $\\sqrt{x^{10}}$, where $x \\ge 0$.",
   "choices": [
    "$x^{5}$",
    "$x^{20}$",
    "$5x$",
    "$x^{100}$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "$\\sqrt{x^{10}} = x^{10/2} = x^{5}$. Halve the exponent for a square root."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "prompt": "Simplify $\\sqrt{x^{2}}$ when $x$ could be any real number.",
   "choices": [
    "$|x|$",
    "$x$",
    "$x^{2}$",
    "$\\pm x$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "An even index always gives a non-negative result, so $\\sqrt{x^{2}} = |x|$ — the absolute value is required unless you are told $x \\ge 0$."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "prompt": "Simplify $\\sqrt{48x^{5}}$, where $x \\ge 0$.",
   "choices": [
    "$4x^{2}\\sqrt{3x}$",
    "$12x^{2}\\sqrt{2x}$",
    "$4x^{3}\\sqrt{3}$",
    "$16x\\sqrt{3x}$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "$48x^{5} = 16x^{4} \\cdot 3x$, and $\\sqrt{16x^{4}} = 4x^{2}$, so the result is $4x^{2}\\sqrt{3x}$."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "easy",
   "prompt": "Simplify $3\\sqrt{5} + 7\\sqrt{5}$.",
   "choices": [
    "$10\\sqrt{5}$",
    "$10\\sqrt{10}$",
    "$21\\sqrt{5}$",
    "$10$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "Like radicals add like terms: $3\\sqrt{5} + 7\\sqrt{5} = (3+7)\\sqrt{5} = 10\\sqrt{5}$. The radicand never changes."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "prompt": "Simplify $\\sqrt{18} + \\sqrt{8}$.",
   "choices": [
    "$5\\sqrt{2}$",
    "$\\sqrt{26}$",
    "$2\\sqrt{13}$",
    "$6\\sqrt{2}$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "Simplify first: $\\sqrt{18} = 3\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{8} = 2\\sqrt{2}$, so the sum is $5\\sqrt{2}$. You may never add radicands."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "prompt": "Simplify $\\sqrt{75} - \\sqrt{12}$.",
   "choices": [
    "$3\\sqrt{3}$",
    "$\\sqrt{63}$",
    "$7\\sqrt{3}$",
    "$63$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "$\\sqrt{75} = 5\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{12} = 2\\sqrt{3}$, so the difference is $(5-2)\\sqrt{3} = 3\\sqrt{3}$."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "easy",
   "prompt": "Simplify $\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{12}$.",
   "choices": [
    "$6$",
    "$36$",
    "$3\\sqrt{12}$",
    "$2\\sqrt{3}$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "The Product Property gives $\\sqrt{3 \\cdot 12} = \\sqrt{36} = 6$."
  },
  {
   "type": "mcq",
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "prompt": "Simplify $(2\\sqrt{5})(3\\sqrt{10})$.",
   "choices": [
    "$30\\sqrt{2}$",
    "$6\\sqrt{50}$",
    "$5\\sqrt{15}$",
    "$6\\sqrt{15}$"
   ],
   "answer": "A",
   "explanation": "Multiply outsides and insides: $6\\sqrt{50} = 6 \\cdot 5\\sqrt{2} = 30\\sqrt{2}$. Always simplify the result."
  },
  {
